{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"airy-starchy-muntjac","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe public CLI and Python library support relation-specific unlink so callers can remove exactly one edge when the same ticket pair carries multiple relations. The registered MCP unlink_tickets tool accepts only id1 and id2 and delegates rebar.unlink without relation. FastMCP therefore advertises no relation field, drops one supplied by a caller, and executes the pair-scoped fallback, which removes the most-recent edge rather than the requested edge.\n\nThis was left explicitly out of scope by closed bug alkaline-lemon-copperhead, which added relation-specific unlink to the shared core, CLI, and library. The signed surface-parity ruling now requires supported write operations to remain in lockstep across CLI, library, and MCP unless an explicit current divergence is documented; none was found for relation-specific unlink.\n\n## Reproduction\nCreate two different relations between the same source and target. Call MCP unlink_tickets with relation naming the older edge. The live schema omits relation, the adapter receives only id1/id2, and the pair-scoped fallback removes the most-recent edge instead.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] MCP unlink_tickets exposes optional relation with the same type/default as rebar.unlink.\n- [ ] A supplied relation is forwarded unchanged and removes exactly that edge while preserving the other relation.\n- [ ] An omitted relation preserves the documented pair-scoped most-recent fallback.\n- [ ] The live MCP schema advertises relation.\n- [ ] Focused MCP/link tests pass.\n- [ ] make lint passes.\n- [ ] make typecheck passes.","id":"88b9-c847-3a2e-4c63","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["mcp","parity","links"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP unlink_tickets cannot target a specific relation"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787086578886175001,"uuid":"90383280-e042-4193-9a7a-4912ff8b16e4"}